            <ArticleTitle>Clinical variables predicting inappropriate use of implantable cardioverter-defibrillator in patients with coronary heart disease or nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>271-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inappropriate therapy is a common clinical problem in recipients of implantable cardioverter-defibrillators (ICDs). The present study evaluated whether clinical characteristics could predict inappropriate ICD therapy due to atrial tachyarrhythmias in a series of 260 patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
